# Docker build context excludes, for tools/ci/*.Dockerfile.
#
# The context is the repository root, and those images build the project from
# scratch the way README says a person would. Everything listed here is host
# state that would make them test something else instead -- in most cases by
# silently SKIPPING work rather than by failing, which is the dangerous kind.

# Phase 4's sentinel (Makefile's DEPS_SENTINEL). Its mere presence, whatever the
# contents, makes `make` skip the entire dependency install; the build then gets
# all the way to `Library "basis" not found` before anyone notices.
.deps-installed

# The host's local opam switch: absolute host paths throughout, and it satisfies
# the phase 1-2 sentinels with a switch the container cannot use.
_opam/
**/_opam/

# Dune's cache, keyed to that same host switch.
_build/
**/_build/

# The 24MB executable that `make build` is supposed to produce in there.
/stelf

# Absent from a clean checkout, but anyone who has run `make lock` has one, and
# shipping it flips dune into package management mode -- a different dependency
# resolution path than the one CI is meant to exercise.
dune.lock/

# Deliberately NOT excluded:
#   .git/    Makefile phase 3 runs `git submodule update`, which needs a real
#            repository; the submodules' .git files are relative gitlinks, so
#            they survive the copy.
#   basis/   a workspace member the build genuinely requires, and
#   twelf/   excluding either only makes the container re-clone it over the
#            network -- slower, and it makes the build need the network at all.
